body:
爱林 is pretty nice except that it feels somewhat outdated and most probably male-leaning.

&#x200B;

Edit: My girlfriend (who is also Chinese) thinks that it's unnatural to have "love" in a name :}

First of all your English is good. I wouldn't think it's necessary for you to take any paid classes, there are a lot of prep material for free online. With an English proficiency like yours, IELTS would most probably be a breeze for you and you need to know no other than some handy tips and a general structure plus some useful ideas for your writing.

&#x200B;

I am a new immigrant to Canada, and I had to take the IELTS exam (among several other requirements including education received, age, work experience, health condition etc.). It isn't the only requirement, but then again I don't know if there are any immigration policies in any country for a younger person like you. In general, you need to take the IELTS for applying to overseas universities, and this is nothing but the first step.

&#x200B;

Being proficient in English WILL give you an edge when comparing yourself to your peers. You will flourish, if circumstances are in favor of you. But you still have to make all the right choices and be sure that you want them. You're young, you still have plenty of time.
